KEPT.poke(r.held) keeps 'r' (a view the caller handed in) in the global 'KEPT', which every routine reaches, and the build can't compare those later uses with where that view's place is given back: keep an Addr there (the view's .to[Addr](), turned back with .to[@T?]() and a when), make the field an &E? when one holder keeps the value, or hand the view as an argument to the routines that use it
